This directory contains the following:

examples/
meta_attributes.yaml
meta_coordinates.yaml
README  << this file
reference_rcParams.txt
sample_app.yaml
sample_specs.yaml
species_database.yaml

First, sample_app.yaml and sample_specs.yaml contains descriptions
of all the options available in the APP and SPECS files.

The files
    meta_attributes.yaml
    meta_coordinates.yaml
    species_database.yaml
are YAML-file configurations used by Eviz. They should not be modifed.


The file reference_rcParams.txt contains a list of all the available
Matplotlib "rcParams" that can be used in the SPECS file to cutomize plots.

The examples/ subdirectory contains all the sample YAML configurations
used in the online Eviz users guide. Those configurations represent
the data source types that EViz supports.

Note that the config files specify the location of the data as well
as the output path of the visualizations. Both of these paths
are assumed to be in the $HOME directory of the user. The data 
is in

$HOME/data/eviz  (multiple subdirectories will be here)

the output is in

$HOME/scratch/eviz/output  (multiple subdirectories will be here).

In the APP YAML file, these paths are specified as follows:

inputs:
   - name     : ${HOME}/data/eviz/airnow/HourlyAQObs*
     description: 25 μm particulate matter
     reader   : csv
     to_plot  :
        PM25: sc

outputs:
    output_dir: ${HOME}/scratch/eviz/output/airnow
    print_to_file: yes


Change ${HOME} to whatever path works in your case. This can (and should) 
be done via environment variables.

